  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Prep ingredients: Bring a medium saucepan of water to the boil for the noodles. Halve the carrot lengthwise, then thinly slice on an angle. Cut the zucchini into 1cm-thick rounds. Thinly slice the spring onion on an angle. Crush or finely chop 1 garlic clove.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2614174/photos/large/prep_ingredients-269cf52c1c7ca50b52ca27717c990239.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cook noodles: Cook the noodles in the pan of boiling water for 2 mins or until tender. Drain, then rinse under hot water to prevent the noodles from sticking.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2614175/photos/large/marinate_chicken-c02de1b41e78eed206a053376fc8a37d.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Warm tofu: Meanwhile, heat 2 tsp vegetable oil in a medium deep frypan over medium heat. Cook the tofu for 2 mins each side or until golden and warmed through. Remove from the pan.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2614176/photos/large/cook_noodles-9d450d69a043cb20f9e1d4635eb232a0.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cook curry sauce: Heat 2 tsp vegetable oil in the same pan over medium-high heat. Stir-fry the carrot, garlic, half the curry powder and 3 tsp soy sauce for 2 mins or until fragrant. Stir in the zucchini, half the coconut milk, 1 tbs tomato sauce and 180ml (¾ cup) water. Reduce the heat to medium and cook, stirring occasionally, for 5 mins or until the carrot is tender.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2614177/photos/large/stir_fry_chicken-4d60767ea47c889e1b16e35c6e409e6d.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve up: Slice the tofu. Add the noodles and tofu to the curry sauce and gently toss until combined and warmed through. Divide the tofu curry noodles among bowls, scatter over the spring onion and enjoy!",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2614178/photos/large/serve_up-4da13d838ea4e3d449247a87b8a58ac4.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Make it spicy: Like it hot? Kick up the heat a notch or two with a scattering of chopped fresh chilli or chilli flakes.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/2614179/photos/large/make_it_yours-fc6a376f10951e7307daac50e6f2132a.jpeg"
    }
  ]
}
